\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
\section{Introduction}
Graph neural network (GNN) models have become the default for molecular property prediction.
\section{Method}
Our graph neural network (GNN) encoder uses four message-passing layers. Compared with a plain graph neural network (GNN), the gated variant converges faster.
\section{Results}
The graph neural network (GNN) baseline reaches 0.81 AUC, while our graph neural network (GNN) variant reaches 0.87.
\end{document}

